		<h2 id="tokens">Usage tokens</h2>
		<p>
			Read the usage token, not the step:
			<code>--ui-color-border</code>
			, not
			<code>--ui-color-surface-6</code>
			. No loose hex, size or font: if you miss something, it is added to UI. The whole contract is in
			<code>packages/ui/DESIGN.md</code>
			.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/styles/main.css"
			bind:code="examples.themeUse"
		/>
		<DocsApi
			caption="Main tokens"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: '--ui-color-bg / -bg-subtle', type: 'color', description: 'Background of the page and quiet bands.' },
				{ name: '--ui-color-surface / -surface-raised', type: 'color', description: 'Card, panel and table; popover and modal.' },
				{ name: '--ui-color-control / -hover / -active', type: 'color', description: 'Background of a control and its states.' },
				{ name: '--ui-color-text / -text-soft', type: 'color', description: 'Text and secondary text.' },
				{ name: '--ui-color-border / -border-strong / -control-border', type: 'color', description: 'Separators, quiet borders and the border of a field at 3:1 or more.' },
				{ name: '--ui-color-primary / -hover / -contrast', type: 'color', description: 'Main action and the text on it.' },
				{ name: '--ui-color-primary-soft / -text / -border', type: 'color', description: 'A label or a quiet active background, with its text and its border.' },
				{ name: '--ui-color-danger / -soft / -border / -text', type: 'color', description: 'Info, success and warning have the same shape.' },
				{ name: '--ui-font-size-xs … -6xl', type: 'rem', description: 'Text sizes: reading at lg, controls at md, titles from 2xl up.' },
				{ name: '--ui-space-* / --ui-radius-*', type: 'rem', description: 'Space in steps of 0.25rem and radii from xs to xl.' },
				{ name: '--ui-control-height-sm / -md / -lg', type: 'rem', description: 'Heights of the controls, which grow by themselves with a touch pointer.' },
				{ name: '--ui-duration-* / --ui-ease-*', type: 'time', description: 'Motion: fast for color, base and slow for a panel.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="scale">Fluid scale</h2>
		<p>
			The interface grows with the screen in one place, the global base: 16 px up to 1440, 18 px at 2560 and 21 px at 3840, always from the font size of the browser. Every token is in
			<code>rem</code>
			, so they grow together. What is written in
			<code>px</code>
			does not grow.
			<code>{'ui: { base: false }'}</code>
			removes the base, and the scale with it.
		</p>
		<h2 id="brand">Your brand</h2>
		<p>
			The sheets of
			<code>app/styles</code>
			load after the module: override the steps of a scale and everything that reads them changes with them.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/styles/main.css"
			bind:code="examples.themeCss"
		/>
		<p>
			If your site already has its variables,
			<code>ui.tokens</code>
			accepts CSS values or references to them, and each key assigns its
			<code>--ui-*</code>
			tokens.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="meeko.config.ts"
			bind:code="examples.theme"
		/>
		<DocsApi
			caption="Keys of ui.tokens"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'primary / primaryHover / onPrimary', type: 'string', description: '--ui-color-primary, its hover and the text on it.' },
				{ name: 'accentSoft / accentText', type: 'string', description: 'Backgrounds and text of active states: --ui-color-primary-soft and -text.' },
				{ name: 'surface / surfaceHover', type: 'string', description: 'Surfaces and controls, and their states.' },
				{ name: 'text / textSoft / muted', type: 'string', description: 'Main and secondary text.' },
				{ name: 'border / borderStrong', type: 'string', description: 'Separators and outlines.' },
				{ name: 'focus / danger', type: 'string', description: 'Keyboard focus and errors.' },
				{ name: 'font / radius', type: 'string', description: 'Font family and base radius.' },
				{ name: 'controlHeight / controlPadding', type: 'string', description: 'Dimensions of the actions.' },
				{ name: 'controlWeight / controlFontSize', type: 'string', description: 'Weight and text size of the actions.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="defaults">Default values</h2>
		<p>
			<code>ui.defaults</code>
			accepts
			<code>button</code>
			,
			<code>link</code>
			and
			<code>card</code>
			. The priority is: explicit props, application defaults and base values. Defaults are isolated per application and SSR request.
		</p>
		<h2 id="messages">Texts and languages</h2>
		<p>
			The few texts components paint on their own (the close button of
			<code>UIModal</code>
			, the empty state of
			<code>UITable</code>
			and
			<code>UICombobox</code>
			, the names of
			<code>UIThemeToggle</code>
			) come in Spanish and English. With
			<code>@meekojs/i18n</code>
			they follow the language of the document, without any configuration. Without that module,
			<code>ui.locale</code>
			chooses the language; Spanish by default.
			<code>ui.messages</code>
			overrides texts or adds other languages.
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.messages" />
		<p>
			A prop or a snippet of the component always win over these texts. What a language lacks comes from its base language (
			<code>pt</code>
			for
			<code>pt-BR</code>
			), from
			<code>ui.locale</code>
			and, last, from Spanish. The server and the client choose the same text, so hydration changes nothing.
		</p>
		<p>
			The types
			<code>UIOptions</code>
			,
			<code>UITokens</code>
			and
			<code>UIDefaults</code>
			are exported from
			<code>@meekojs/ui</code>
			.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
